**Status Update 20.07.2026**

Company data ruled out: it is customer-owned (not company owned), so it cannot be used as the basis for a published thesis due to legal/IP constraints.

CWRU Bearing Dataset was considered as a fallback but deprioritized per supervisor feedback: it provides pre-processed, low-dimensional features (not raw device logs) and is heavily saturated in existing literature, limiting novelty.

Decision: proceeding with the GWDG HPC Log Dataset -> [https://zenodo.org/records/19052367](https://pad.gwdg.de/_link?url=https%3A%2F%2Fzenodo.org%2Frecords%2F19052367&note=Etgms5l1RayhbrPnIm64EA)

- Aligns directly with the approved thesis topic (device log anomaly detection)

- Plan: log preprocessing -> semi-complex/hybrid feature engineering -> lightweight anomaly detection model -> edge deployment comparison

- Naturally supports TinyML/compression techniques

